 a long time  favorite and there are many reasons why  i like it it's a sit stand desk and it's  also on rolling casters so really this  desk is flexible in however way i want  to use it in case i wanted to move it to  like a different part of the room or if  i wanted to be standing and sitting and  alternating throughout the day and in  terms of the things that are on my desk  i have several videos where i've talked  about that so i'll link them right here  in the card and the description box down  below but yeah things like my monitor my  computer my keyboard and mouse desk mat  how i mount my computer the speakers  charging ports lighting all of those  things i've spent like a meticulous  amount of time choosing each one  intentionally to really fit my needs so  yeah i won't go into that too much  because there's literally entire videos  about that so give those a watch so the  next zone that i want to talk about is  part of my desk area is the bookshelf so  this is positioned to the left of my  desk and it kind of serves as almost  like a privacy screen as well my door is  right behind that and so without it i  see my dogs and my husband walking by  and whoever else is at home and  it's kind of distracting honestly and so  having a bookshelf there so that i can  really focus on what's going on in front  of me at my desk without being  distracted about what's going on outside  has been really nice the bookshelf is  the ikea calyx uh which is like the cube  shelf that everybody has ikea always  sells them it comes in so many different  colors we actually brought it from our  other house where it served a different  purpose but i thought it would be really  perfect here and it has been it's been  some really great like visible storage  and decoration and again the privacy  part has been really nice the next zone  of my desk area is behind the desk now  this is a recent improvement i talked  about this in my desk accessories video  but i added these sound tiles from felt  right as well as this floating shelf to  give the space a little bit more visual  interest before i put this up it was  just like a blank white wall which is  totally fine but i wanted to add some  visual interest some color some texture  because i'm sitting facing this wall  like most of the day and i really liked  the colors of these felt right tiles and  i wanted a place to put one of my plants  and to be honest with you putting this  right behind my desk has kind of given  my desk like an identity it's kind of  like okay this is like a whole area that  is set because look at how well it's  decorated so  i really think it's brought everything  together and then the last part of my  desk area that i want to talk about is  my storage cabinet to the right of my  desk this is also a pretty recent  addition i got this from ikea i forgot  which one it's called but i wanted just  some more storage and some easy access  to storage for things like pens and  pencils and stationery and laptops and  books and stuff like that i also really  like that it provides some storage on  top right now i have my printer on there  but i genuinely and generally don't  really want to put that much stuff on my  desk i want to keep my desk area itself  pretty clean and so having some extra  areas to just place stuff on top of has  been really nice and before we move on i  want to say a quick thank you to helix  sleep helix sleep is a company that  creates premium mattresses customized to  fit your needs shipped directly to your  door i myself own two helix sleep  mattresses and they are legitimately the  best mattresses i've ever had they're so  good i get great night sleep from them  every night genuinely a really really  great mattress company helix's sleep  quiz matches you with the perfect  mattress based on your body type and  sleep preferences i myself am kind of  like a back and side sleeper and i  prefer like a medium firm mattress and  so the one that i have is the dusk luxe